WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.257 --> 00:00:03.322
- The beach is not a very safe space.

00:00:03.322 --> 00:00:05.993
Anyone can relate to feeling
uncomfortable on the beach.

00:00:05.993 --> 00:00:08.334
Men, women, queer, otherwise.

00:00:08.334 --> 00:00:10.400
And it's also a very gendered space,

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:13.239
like the moment you put
your toes in the sand

00:00:13.239 --> 00:00:14.390
you know it and you feel it

00:00:14.390 --> 00:00:16.592
and you know that you have to kind of

00:00:16.592 --> 00:00:18.000
pick one side of the spectrum.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:19.560
Either you're more on the masculine side

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:22.211
or you're more on the feminine side.

00:00:22.211 --> 00:00:23.679
What does that do for everyone that

00:00:23.679 --> 00:00:27.759
doesn't exist on one
clear side or the other?

00:00:27.759 --> 00:00:30.342
(upbeat music)

00:00:34.221 --> 00:00:36.638
(cool music)

00:00:38.443 --> 00:00:39.620
I am Ari Fitz,

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:42.632
and I run a fashion
project called Tomboyish.

00:00:42.632 --> 00:00:44.360
It in so many ways aims

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:46.120
to tackle the way that we see beauty

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:49.369
and the way that we see
masculinity and femininity.

00:00:49.369 --> 00:00:51.232
A couple years ago, I
really started to balance

00:00:51.232 --> 00:00:53.480
my own masculinity and femininity,

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:56.363
and I felt really good,
and I felt like myself.

00:00:56.363 --> 00:00:59.511
I wanted to help other
people get there too.

00:00:59.511 --> 00:01:02.161
To me, getting dressed in the morning

00:01:02.161 --> 00:01:05.164
is kind of like putting
on my suit of armor.

00:01:05.164 --> 00:01:06.429
As a queer person,

00:01:06.429 --> 00:01:08.419
as a woman, as a person of color,

00:01:08.419 --> 00:01:10.221
I feel like there are so many things

00:01:10.221 --> 00:01:12.409
in this world that wants to silence us,

00:01:12.409 --> 00:01:14.232
silence me, minimize me,

00:01:14.232 --> 00:01:17.192
and minimize my experience in this world.

00:01:17.192 --> 00:01:19.061
What we choose to wear signifies that

00:01:19.061 --> 00:01:20.680
we are here, we are present,

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:21.931
and we're not going to be silenced,

00:01:21.931 --> 00:01:24.240
we're not going anywhere.

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:25.073
'Sup, Ben?

00:01:25.997 --> 00:01:27.331
Hey!

00:01:27.331 --> 00:01:29.141
So the project I'm working
on is a really dope,

00:01:29.141 --> 00:01:31.701
super hot lookbook that
features all things

00:01:31.701 --> 00:01:33.701
swimwear for those who don't exist

00:01:33.701 --> 00:01:35.440
on the hyper masculine side or

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:37.756
the hyper feminine side, like myself.

00:01:37.756 --> 00:01:39.301
Because I know what it feels like

00:01:39.301 --> 00:01:43.134
to step out on a beach
and not feel confident.

00:01:45.621 --> 00:01:47.090
We have to get creative.

00:01:47.090 --> 00:01:49.536
We have to find items
that most of the time

00:01:49.536 --> 00:01:51.901
you wouldn't really
think are like swimwear

00:01:51.901 --> 00:01:53.663
or beachwear pieces,

00:01:53.663 --> 00:01:56.739
and we have to make them ours.

00:01:56.739 --> 00:01:58.065
Swim vests,

00:01:58.065 --> 00:02:00.580
also bodysuits.

00:02:00.580 --> 00:02:03.747
And then from there, just accessorize.

00:02:04.838 --> 00:02:08.070
(shouting and laughing)

00:02:08.070 --> 00:02:09.689
It's a beach.

00:02:09.689 --> 00:02:11.950
It's meant to be fun,
it's meant to be light,

00:02:11.950 --> 00:02:12.950
it's summer.

00:02:13.871 --> 00:02:15.969
The stress and the trauma
that people experience

00:02:15.969 --> 00:02:17.437
when they go to a beach is just like,

00:02:17.437 --> 00:02:19.104
it's so unnecessary.

00:02:20.769 --> 00:02:23.049
The more I can do to just
get that out of the way

00:02:23.049 --> 00:02:25.119
and make the beach fun again,

00:02:25.119 --> 00:02:27.871
that means that my job is done.

00:02:27.871 --> 00:02:29.199
Do you, boo, just rock it!

00:02:29.199 --> 00:02:30.055
Just make sure you're like,

00:02:30.055 --> 00:02:31.173
rocking it with like, you know,

00:02:31.173 --> 00:02:32.817
some confidence, and you got it.

00:02:32.817 --> 00:02:35.234
(cool music)

00:02:40.071 --> 00:02:42.071
(chime)

